  "solution": {
    "text": "Is an adiabatic process<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>T</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>V</mi><msup><mi>T</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> as T increase V decreases at non-uniform rate<br /><br />In process <math><mi>a</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>b</mi></math> P = constant as <math><mi>V</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>T</mi></math><br /><br />In process <math><mi>c</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>d</mi></math> <math><msup><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>&#8242;</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo></math> constant s <math><mi>V</mi><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>T</mi></math><br /><br />But since slope of V - T graph <math><mo>&#8733;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />since slope of ab &lt; slope of cd<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />Also in adiabatic process <math><mi>d</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>a</mi></math> as T is increasing V in decreasing<br /><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> P is increasing, so P - V diagram is as below<br /><br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a1963d6d-1d3f-4c22-9fb1-419878818f13-image.png\" style=\"width: 186px; height: 187px;\" />",
